        "pubYear": "2022",
        "abstractText": "<h4>Purpose: </h4> To study vessel density (VD) on Optical Coherence Tomography Angiography (OCTA) at choroid, chorio-capillaries (CC) & various retinal levels in normal population & various stages of dry AMD & how these changes progress with increase in severity of the disease.  <h4>Methods: </h4> Prospective, observational , cross-sectional study done on 252 eyes of 132 patients presenting to tertiary care centre in Central India between February 2021 to January 2022. For study purpose, eyes were divided into 5 groups according to the size and number of the drusen, viz, Group 1: No AMD (<50 years) , Group 2: No AMD ( > 50 years) , Group 3 : Early AMD and Group 4 : Intermediate AMD & Group 5 : Advanced AMD. In all eyes , VD was measured at choroid , CC, Deep capillary plexus (DCP) of retina & superficial capillary plexus (SCP) of retina.  <h4>Results: </h4> There were total 61 males & 71 females in the study . The mean age in case cohort is 61.90 ± 7.97 years with 52 (51.48%) males and 49 (48.51%) females. At choroidal level, the mean vascular density differed significantly across diagnosis types in all the quadrants (p < 0.05). Similar was the observation at CC & DCP level. At SCP level, except in central quadrant, the differences for remaining quadrants were significant across the groups. At SCP & DCP increase in VD is seen in early AMD cohort compared to No AMD (> 50 years) cohort, which showed continuous reduction later in intermediate & advanced AMD cohort.  <h4>Conclusion: </h4> With increase in the severity of disease, significant reduction in VD is also seen in retinal plexuses, along with the changes in choroid & CC. These VD maps may play a role as non-invasive biomarkers for healthy & diseased aging.",
